Short source-landscape note: Ethiopia in 2023 has a dense macroeconomic paper trail around inflation, debt distress, FX reform, fiscal tightening, and reform-program negotiations. The most useful discovery families are official finance/central-bank materials, IMF/World Bank/UNDP diagnostics, debt bulletins, governance/corruption indices, and local investigative reporting. I found more than 30 distinct candidate documents/URLs and kept both favorable and adverse perspectives in view.

